    "note": "Coarse overview of the ITU Region 3 allocations (most of Asia east of Iran, Australasia and the Pacific), derived directly from the ITU Radio Regulations, Edition of 2024, Volume 1 (Articles), Article 5 Table of Frequency Allocations and Article 23, read from the ITU's own PDF at search.itu.int/history/HistoryDigitalCollectionDocLibrary/1.49.48.en.101.pdf. Every band below is the Region 3 column (or a worldwide row) of that table. Points where Region 3 differs from Region 1 or 2: mediumwave runs 526.5-1606.5 kHz on the 9 kHz GE75 raster (Region 2 is 535-1705 kHz on 10 kHz); 160 m amateur is the full 1800-2000 kHz (Region 1 has only 1810-1850); 80 m amateur runs to 3900 kHz (Region 1 stops at 3800); 2 m amateur runs to 148 MHz (Region 1 stops at 146); 6 m amateur is the full 50-54 MHz; and broadcasting is allocated from 87 MHz, not 87.5 MHz. 40 m amateur is 7000-7200 kHz, the same as Region 1 and narrower than Region 2's 7000-7300. Mediumwave channel raster is from the Final Acts of the Regional Administrative LF/MF Broadcasting Conference (Regions 1 and 3), Geneva 1975 (GE75), whose assignments are all integral multiples of 9 kHz. Marine VHF is the RR Appendix 18 channel span (RR 5.226 names 156-157.45 MHz and 160.6-162.05 MHz), rounded outward. INFORMATIONAL ONLY - a display aid, not an authoritative or licensing reference. Deliberately coarser than the per-country plans: many bands carry country-specific footnotes that are not modelled, and several Region 3 administrations depart from the table. JSON has no comment syntax, so this note lives in the data; the loader ignores unknown keys.",
